      "message": "### Simplification: Encapsulate Endianness in the Protocol Structs\n\nIn `bootrom.cc`, functions like `GetBootromInfo` and `GetFlashInfo` manually mutate the struct fields after reading them to handle endianness:\n\n```c\ninfo_res-\u003eversion \u003d FromLittleEndian(info_res-\u003eversion);\ninfo_res-\u003emax_cmd_size \u003d FromLittleEndian(info_res-\u003emax_cmd_size);\n\n```\n\nThis is error-prone; if a new field is added to the struct in the future, the developer might forget to add the swap logic in the caller.\n\n**The Simplification:** Move the endian-swapping logic directly into the structs defined in `bootrom_protocol.h`. Add a simple `Unpack()` or `ToHost()` member function to the struct itself.\n\n```c\nstruct BootromInfoResponse {\n  uint32_t version;\n  uint32_t max_cmd_size;\n  uint32_t max_fw_upgrade_size;\n\n  void ToHost() {\n    version \u003d egis::FromLittleEndian(version);\n    max_cmd_size \u003d egis::FromLittleEndian(max_cmd_size);\n    max_fw_upgrade_size \u003d egis::FromLittleEndian(max_fw_upgrade_size);\n  }\n} __attribute__((packed));\n\n```",
